WEBVTT

00:53.428 --> 00:54.471
Good morning.

00:57.390 --> 00:58.725
Good morning.

01:12.238 --> 01:14.157
Here. Enjoy.

01:15.492 --> 01:17.035
Everything looks delicious.

01:17.535 --> 01:19.162
I can really eat all this?

01:19.245 --> 01:20.121
Yeah.

01:20.205 --> 01:22.457
Because I'm not going home for Chuseok,

01:22.540 --> 01:24.793
eomma brought me tons of side dishes

01:24.876 --> 01:26.753
and snacks that I love.

01:28.671 --> 01:30.131
Chuseok?

01:34.219 --> 01:36.638
It's kind of like Obon in Japan.

01:37.722 --> 01:38.932
I see.

01:39.432 --> 01:42.101
Speaking of which,
are you going home for Obon?

01:47.774 --> 01:50.360
I'm still thinking about it.

01:53.738 --> 01:55.907
Let's eat before it gets cold.

01:57.617 --> 01:59.119
Thank you for the food.

01:59.953 --> 02:01.621
Thank you for the food.

02:06.960 --> 02:08.711
This is good.

02:15.552 --> 02:16.719
Kkulmat.

02:20.515 --> 02:22.475
What? Was that wrong?

02:22.559 --> 02:24.978
That's what you say
when it's delicious, right--

02:26.396 --> 02:27.564
Kkulmat?

02:27.647 --> 02:28.857
Yeah, that!

02:29.440 --> 02:31.901
That's right. It's right, but…

02:32.485 --> 02:33.945
You're too cute.

02:35.238 --> 02:37.907
The fact that you're
trying to remember Korean words

02:38.408 --> 02:39.409
makes me happy.

02:40.660 --> 02:41.494
I'm glad.

02:42.996 --> 02:44.164
Let's eat.

02:48.918 --> 02:50.962
I ate a little too much.

02:51.462 --> 02:54.924
You basically ate
all the seaweed soup, after all.

03:12.650 --> 03:14.611
Oh, sorry! I couldn't help myself…

03:16.738 --> 03:18.656
Did you want one too?

03:19.157 --> 03:19.991
Huh?

03:20.074 --> 03:21.284
All right…

03:23.870 --> 03:25.455
I'll shu… sho…

03:26.706 --> 03:28.124
I'll share some with you.

03:29.626 --> 03:30.627
Thank you.

03:30.710 --> 03:32.921
NURUNGJI

03:34.172 --> 03:36.883
Can I ask what flavor this is?

03:39.344 --> 03:40.929
A warm flavor.

03:41.554 --> 03:43.139
A warm flavor?

03:43.223 --> 03:46.476
This is my favorite candy.

03:46.559 --> 03:49.187
It lifts my spirits
especially when I'm feeling down,

03:49.270 --> 03:50.730
so you have to try it.

03:51.898 --> 03:52.982
I'll look forward to it.

03:53.858 --> 03:57.237
Thank you for sharing
such a precious candy with me.

04:02.116 --> 04:03.576
What's wrong?

04:46.494 --> 04:49.539
BIG BRO

04:56.587 --> 04:57.588
Hello?

05:05.179 --> 05:07.974
This is route number TE301.

05:08.558 --> 05:11.144
Last stop is Nagano Station.

05:13.479 --> 05:15.940
We will arrive at Nagano Station

05:16.024 --> 05:18.568
at approximately 5:05.

05:22.030 --> 05:24.741
We will now turn off the lights…

06:43.277 --> 06:45.238
- You can do it!
- Taiga!

06:45.321 --> 06:48.116
- Run! Go!
- Run Taiga!

06:48.199 --> 06:49.158
You can do it!

06:49.242 --> 06:50.952
Taiga!

07:03.714 --> 07:04.966
Taiga.

07:05.049 --> 07:06.676
You're off the team.

07:17.228 --> 07:19.480
Don't look so depressed.

07:20.189 --> 07:23.151
You were just a reserve member
this one time.

07:23.651 --> 07:25.278
I'm not depressed…

07:27.864 --> 07:29.699
If you have the time to be sulking,

07:29.782 --> 07:32.034
shouldn't you be practicing?

08:05.651 --> 08:07.612
Food is ready. Eat up.

08:07.695 --> 08:09.280
- Thank you.
- All right.

08:14.327 --> 08:16.120
I made the onigiri small for you.

08:16.204 --> 08:17.413
It's easier to eat that way.

08:18.915 --> 08:21.667
Right? Make sure you eat a lot.

08:21.751 --> 08:23.753
Here. Do your best.

08:23.836 --> 08:25.087
Thank you.

08:26.088 --> 08:27.632
Just don't get hurt.

08:31.385 --> 08:34.472
Forty-seven, forty-eight, forty-nine,

08:34.555 --> 08:36.432
fifty, fifty-one…

08:50.780 --> 08:52.490
- Bye, Taiga.
- Bye.

08:52.573 --> 08:53.449
Bye.

08:53.950 --> 08:56.202
- Coach says he's treating us today.
- No way!

08:56.786 --> 08:58.329
How much will that be?

09:13.386 --> 09:14.554
5000 meters.

09:14.637 --> 09:16.389
Ready… Go!

09:22.228 --> 09:26.482
Forty-eight, forty-nine, fifty, fifty-one…

09:26.566 --> 09:28.818
First place, 13 minutes 51 seconds.

09:44.667 --> 09:45.585
Coach.

09:48.087 --> 09:49.005
Taiga.

09:52.091 --> 09:54.218
I understand that you're working hard.

09:55.094 --> 09:55.970
But you know…

09:57.763 --> 09:58.931
you're not the only one

10:00.224 --> 10:01.517
who is working hard.

10:09.567 --> 10:12.445
21. HASE TAIGA

10:19.118 --> 10:22.413
The dorm cafeteria is understaffed.

10:23.748 --> 10:25.916
So from now on, go and help them.

10:29.754 --> 10:32.423
- Man, that's brutal.
- The cafeteria?

10:32.506 --> 10:33.341
Poor guy.

10:33.424 --> 10:35.843
He got an endorsement and he's a reserve?

10:39.013 --> 10:40.222
You don't have to come out.

10:41.057 --> 10:42.892
I'll contact you once I get to Tokyo.

10:45.061 --> 10:45.978
Taiga.

10:48.731 --> 10:50.441
Are you really sure?

10:52.151 --> 10:53.069
Huh?

10:54.195 --> 10:55.488
You know,

10:55.571 --> 10:57.907
you've loved running
since you were a child.

10:57.990 --> 11:00.660
You would run around all day if I let you.

11:01.827 --> 11:03.120
I bet you still want to run--

11:03.204 --> 11:05.039
Enough about track.

11:10.544 --> 11:13.589
There are a ton of people who are
on a completely different level than me.

11:15.132 --> 11:17.802
I tried to run as fast as I could,
but it was pointless.

11:19.261 --> 11:20.805
Just "liking" it…

11:22.515 --> 11:23.849
was not enough.

11:27.269 --> 11:29.647
That's all there is to it.

11:31.273 --> 11:32.942
Don't make me talk about it anymore.

11:34.068 --> 11:34.985
Okay…

11:36.612 --> 11:37.863
You're right…

11:41.283 --> 11:42.618
It's okay.

11:42.701 --> 11:44.829
You didn't fail.

11:45.496 --> 11:47.873
You have a whole life ahead of you.

11:50.042 --> 11:51.127
Don't be anxious.

11:51.961 --> 11:55.005
Find something only you can do,
and do it at your own pace.

11:56.757 --> 11:57.716
I'm sure…

11:59.009 --> 12:02.430
As long as you try your best,
that's enough.

12:09.478 --> 12:10.771
Bye.

13:34.647 --> 13:35.606
Welcome home!

13:36.190 --> 13:37.233
Taiga!

13:38.776 --> 13:39.902
I'm home.

13:44.198 --> 13:45.991
You don't have time.
Hurry and get changed.

13:51.539 --> 13:52.540
Well then…

13:53.123 --> 13:55.084
I'd like to thank everyone

13:55.167 --> 13:57.670
who took time out of their busy schedules
to be here

13:58.295 --> 13:59.713
for our father's 13th anniversary.

14:01.006 --> 14:01.840
May he rest in peace.

14:02.341 --> 14:03.259
- May he rest in peace.
- May he rest in peace.

14:08.681 --> 14:09.515
Yuji,

14:09.598 --> 14:11.934
- thank you for today.
- No, thank you.

14:13.894 --> 14:15.771
I must say, Masa, I'm so glad

14:15.854 --> 14:17.356
- I asked you for help.
- It was nothing.

14:17.439 --> 14:18.941
Good thing you did.

14:19.024 --> 14:22.862
Although, it is more than
90% a loan rather than "my home."

14:22.945 --> 14:26.198
- That can't be helped.
- But I think you bought at a good time.

14:26.282 --> 14:28.909
The interest rates
and price of land were low.

14:30.160 --> 14:31.787
Hey, Haruto.

14:31.871 --> 14:34.874
- If Masa says so, that must be true.
- Yeah.

14:35.958 --> 14:37.585
- Right?
- If it's Masa.

14:37.668 --> 14:39.545
- Come here.
- You should all go to him for help.

14:39.628 --> 14:40.838
That's right.

14:43.257 --> 14:45.134
As expected…

14:45.217 --> 14:46.635
Come over here. Up we go.

14:49.263 --> 14:52.266
REMARKABLE!
RENEWS HIGHEST RANKING FOR THE PREFECTURE

15:27.885 --> 15:29.053
I'll help.

15:30.471 --> 15:31.805
Thank you.

15:51.659 --> 15:54.745
Dad liked wood ear mushrooms, didn't he?

16:03.796 --> 16:04.880
Oh!

16:04.964 --> 16:06.924
You're good!

16:07.007 --> 16:08.676
I do this every day.

16:13.138 --> 16:14.932
- I'll take this.
- Sure.

16:53.887 --> 16:54.805
So?

16:56.515 --> 16:57.433
Huh?

16:58.017 --> 17:00.644
What are you planning to do
with your life?

17:05.149 --> 17:06.358
Actually,

17:07.067 --> 17:10.362
the restaurant I'm working at right now
is pretty nice.

17:11.822 --> 17:15.242
You said it was
a privately run izakaya, right?

17:15.743 --> 17:16.660
Yeah.

17:17.286 --> 17:19.621
The owner and I run it on our own.

17:20.456 --> 17:22.458
And he relies on me a lot.

17:24.835 --> 17:26.211
You're the only part-timer?

17:27.296 --> 17:28.422
Yeah.

17:28.505 --> 17:30.674
Come on, he relies on you

17:31.341 --> 17:33.010
because he has nobody else.

17:35.721 --> 17:36.805
Don't get the wrong idea.

17:38.891 --> 17:41.310
Anyone can do your job.

17:47.775 --> 17:50.235
- Dad!
- What's wrong?

17:50.736 --> 17:53.989
You little baby. Up we go. All right.

17:54.073 --> 17:57.451
Where's your mom? Let's go.

18:03.582 --> 18:06.627
But I guess what he said is right.

18:07.127 --> 18:08.837
No offense to your brother,

18:08.921 --> 18:11.090
but I think he's wrong.

18:11.799 --> 18:16.178
Both Tanomi, and the owner
really need you.

18:17.930 --> 18:19.473
You think so?

18:21.058 --> 18:22.768
Not only are you a good cook,

18:23.352 --> 18:26.021
but you're also good
at explaining the menu,

18:26.105 --> 18:28.398
and you're always smiling,
no matter how busy it is.

18:31.235 --> 18:34.363
But it doesn't have to be me…

18:35.114 --> 18:38.242
Just like he said, anybody can do that.

18:39.034 --> 18:40.494
That's not true.

18:42.454 --> 18:44.289
I don't think many people

18:44.373 --> 18:46.917
can keep that attitude up day after day,

18:47.417 --> 18:48.877
like it's nothing.

18:50.087 --> 18:52.673
It's something to be proud of. I know it.

18:57.261 --> 19:00.430
Being consistent
over a long period of time,

19:01.598 --> 19:03.183
is the most powerful trait.

19:03.892 --> 19:05.185
Am I wrong?

19:25.873 --> 19:27.374
I believe

19:28.667 --> 19:31.128
that your training right now
will not be wasted.

20:00.199 --> 20:01.742
NURUNGJI

20:12.461 --> 20:13.754
She's right…

20:15.297 --> 20:16.506
It's a warm flavor.

20:35.317 --> 20:38.737
Hey, where were you? Hurry up and help us.

20:39.738 --> 20:40.864
Hey…

20:44.034 --> 20:44.910
um…

20:46.954 --> 20:49.831
Right now, I'm training.

20:50.832 --> 20:51.667
Huh?

20:52.334 --> 20:53.961
It's true that right now,

20:54.586 --> 20:55.629
I'm just a part-timer

20:56.672 --> 20:58.799
and the work that I'm doing

20:59.591 --> 21:02.761
can arguably be done by anybody.

21:04.096 --> 21:05.264
But…

21:06.765 --> 21:10.102
if I keep pursuing
this thing that anybody can do,

21:11.061 --> 21:12.604
in the end…

21:14.690 --> 21:17.901
I think it will turn into something
that only I can do.

21:21.321 --> 21:22.698
That's why, right now,

21:23.865 --> 21:26.243
I want to treasure
the days I spend training.

21:28.412 --> 21:30.622
I want to make a steady effort,
and continue cooking.

21:33.667 --> 21:34.584
I just…

21:36.753 --> 21:38.547
wanted to tell you that.

21:51.435 --> 21:53.270
What if it falls through again?

21:54.396 --> 21:55.230
What?

21:55.981 --> 21:58.859
Are you prepared to keep at it
until the very end?

22:00.861 --> 22:01.862
Prepared?

22:06.074 --> 22:07.326
That…

22:10.579 --> 22:11.747
I don't know.

22:16.126 --> 22:18.420
In the end, you haven't changed at all.

22:21.965 --> 22:23.508
If you dillydally,

22:23.592 --> 22:26.136
and continue something without resolve,
you're only wasting time.

22:27.179 --> 22:30.849
Not to mention,
you already made a detour once.

22:53.163 --> 22:54.039
‪Who's that?

22:54.122 --> 22:55.332
My Senior.

22:58.668 --> 22:59.753
Nice to meet you.

23:00.504 --> 23:01.797
I'm Kang Jun-ho.

23:03.840 --> 23:04.925
Let me carry those.

23:09.596 --> 23:12.099
Thanks for coming
even though it's your day off.

23:12.182 --> 23:14.142
It's nothing.

23:17.813 --> 23:18.897
Jun-ho,

23:19.523 --> 23:21.274
are you dating anyone?

23:21.358 --> 23:22.442
What?

23:24.486 --> 23:25.737
No, I'm not.

23:27.531 --> 23:29.699
Well then, what do you do for work?

23:29.783 --> 23:31.827
What are your parents like?

23:31.910 --> 23:32.994
What do you like to eat?

23:33.078 --> 23:35.163
Mom, please stop.

23:35.247 --> 23:36.331
I work

23:36.832 --> 23:39.709
at a foreign-owned trading company.

23:39.793 --> 23:41.670
My parents are civil servants.

23:41.753 --> 23:42.796
My hobby is playing soccer.

23:43.380 --> 23:46.049
I love sundae gukbap.

23:46.133 --> 23:48.093
Please ask me anything.

23:48.176 --> 23:50.220
What is your MBTI type?

23:51.221 --> 23:52.347
You know about MBTI too?

23:52.430 --> 23:53.807
What type of girl do you like?

23:53.890 --> 23:56.309
- Someone like you.
- You have good taste!

23:56.393 --> 23:57.561
NARITA INTERNATIONAL AIRPORT

23:57.644 --> 23:59.729
Jun-ho seems like a nice person.

23:59.813 --> 24:02.524
You're not thinking about
doing anything weird, are you?

24:02.607 --> 24:05.861
Jun-ho and I are like brother and sister.

24:10.448 --> 24:13.160
I have something to say, so sit down.

24:18.582 --> 24:21.668
A part-time instructor position opened up

24:21.751 --> 24:24.004
at a vocational school
in Gyeonggi Province.

24:24.087 --> 24:27.591
Once you graduate, work there.

24:28.842 --> 24:30.177
Wait a second.

24:30.927 --> 24:35.140
I've been working hard
to become an animator.

24:35.223 --> 24:36.349
I know that.

24:36.433 --> 24:37.434
But you can't

24:37.517 --> 24:41.646
become one
just because you want to, right?

24:41.730 --> 24:44.191
And plus, you yourself

24:44.274 --> 24:47.527
were saying that you don't know
if you have talent.

24:48.111 --> 24:49.529
Did you forget that?

24:51.615 --> 24:54.117
Why do you have to go out of your way

24:54.868 --> 24:57.287
to choose a difficult path?

25:00.749 --> 25:02.000
Rin, listen to me.

25:02.083 --> 25:04.336
The most important thing

25:04.419 --> 25:08.131
is to lead a stable life.

25:08.215 --> 25:11.426
Trust your mother, okay?

25:11.509 --> 25:13.678
Just do as I say.

25:14.554 --> 25:18.350
You only have half a year
until graduation anyway.

25:25.106 --> 25:26.107
Taiga.

25:26.900 --> 25:28.401
You don't have to rush.

25:33.531 --> 25:37.118
You don't have to do
anything extraordinary.

25:39.287 --> 25:42.249
You just do
what you can to the best of your ability.

25:47.128 --> 25:48.338
Nobody…

25:50.131 --> 25:52.342
expects anything from me anymore, huh?

25:57.931 --> 26:00.433
I think that hurts the most.

26:11.278 --> 26:13.196
But Mom…

26:15.240 --> 26:16.283
Thank you.

27:00.410 --> 27:02.329
All right.

27:06.750 --> 27:07.709
Okay.

27:08.585 --> 27:09.586
What?

27:10.128 --> 27:12.130
Taiga? What's wrong?

27:12.213 --> 27:14.799
TANOMI

27:15.925 --> 27:17.927
I wasn't able

27:18.720 --> 27:21.389
to stand up to my mother or my brother.

27:24.768 --> 27:25.685
Thank you.

27:28.021 --> 27:30.148
My brother may be right…

27:32.108 --> 27:33.610
In the end,

27:35.111 --> 27:36.863
I haven't changed.

27:37.697 --> 27:40.617
No, I might actually be worse.

27:43.244 --> 27:44.537
What do you mean?

27:47.290 --> 27:49.042
I'm 27 already,

27:49.667 --> 27:53.004
but I've accomplished nothing
and have nothing

27:54.297 --> 27:55.632
to call my own.

27:57.759 --> 27:59.552
I'm so pathetic.

28:08.144 --> 28:09.062
Taiga.

28:09.938 --> 28:11.481
Do you have time tomorrow morning?

28:17.404 --> 28:20.031
NARITA CITY WHOLESALE MARKET

28:26.621 --> 28:27.747
BELL PEPPERS 100 YEN

28:27.831 --> 28:29.582
MELONS

28:29.666 --> 28:30.708
BELL PEPPERS

28:30.792 --> 28:32.252
SHINE MUSCAT

28:32.335 --> 28:35.171
ORGANIC VEGETABLES - FRESH VEGETABLES

28:35.255 --> 28:38.675
All right, maybe I'll make corn tempura
or something.

28:38.758 --> 28:39.634
Oh?

28:39.718 --> 28:41.553
- Shige?
- Hey.

28:41.636 --> 28:43.138
You're not alone today?

28:43.221 --> 28:45.181
This is Taiga, he works at my place.

28:45.765 --> 28:47.976
This is Mr. Nagamori,
who I've known for over 30 years.

28:48.560 --> 28:50.437
I'm Hase. Nice to meet you.

28:52.105 --> 28:53.523
The one you've been talking about?

28:54.357 --> 28:56.109
I look forward to seeing more of you.

28:57.318 --> 28:59.529
- How's today's cabbage?
- They're from Tsumagoi.

29:00.822 --> 29:03.908
- Hey, Ito.
- Hey, Shige.

29:03.992 --> 29:05.368
What's in today?

29:05.452 --> 29:08.997
Today, we have nice flounder from Aomori.

29:09.497 --> 29:11.708
- That's great. This must be…
- This is…

29:11.791 --> 29:13.960
- Two kilograms?
- Yes, 2.6 kilograms.

29:14.043 --> 29:16.379
- 2.6?
- Yes. It's very fresh.

29:16.463 --> 29:19.048
- I'll come by later.
- Okay. Thank you.

29:19.132 --> 29:19.966
FOR TANOMI

29:20.633 --> 29:22.177
Here. Flying squid.

29:23.344 --> 29:24.637
For squid,

29:24.721 --> 29:28.308
you can tell that it's fresh
when it's dark and shiny, not faded.

29:28.892 --> 29:30.185
I'll pay, so wait for me.

29:30.268 --> 29:32.437
- Okay.
- Excuse me.

30:26.157 --> 30:28.660
Everything was really cool.

30:29.744 --> 30:32.789
You and everyone at the market.

30:36.334 --> 30:38.628
I quit high school before graduating.

30:45.260 --> 30:49.264
I started working as a cook
just to make ends meet.

30:50.890 --> 30:53.017
And I just kind of continued
down that path,

30:53.101 --> 30:54.894
and found myself here.

31:00.108 --> 31:02.861
Both people and things change.

31:07.407 --> 31:10.368
Yesterday, you said that you had
nothing to call your own.

31:11.119 --> 31:12.704
But is that really so?

31:31.180 --> 31:33.933
All right, should we get some
breakfast or something?

31:35.059 --> 31:37.437
- Yes.
- Down we go.

31:40.273 --> 31:41.274
Welcome back.

31:46.446 --> 31:47.739
It's good to be back.

31:55.413 --> 31:56.998
When my family makes gimbap,

31:57.081 --> 31:59.500
we flavor the rice even before we cook it.

32:05.048 --> 32:07.592
What we put inside is not always the same.

32:07.675 --> 32:09.093
But one thing we always include

32:09.177 --> 32:10.345
is bell pepper.

32:13.014 --> 32:15.183
When I was a kid,

32:15.266 --> 32:17.310
I didn't like eating vegetables,

32:17.894 --> 32:21.147
so eomma cut them up finely
and put them in gimbap.

32:22.523 --> 32:24.692
In Korea, everyone brings gimbap

32:24.776 --> 32:27.403
on field trips and sports days.

32:29.572 --> 32:30.949
So on those days,

32:31.032 --> 32:34.202
the whole house
smells good from morning and all day long.

32:34.702 --> 32:36.871
- Sounds like the best morning ever.
- Yeah.

32:37.705 --> 32:39.874
So from the moment you wake up,

32:39.958 --> 32:42.251
you know that it's going to be a good day

32:42.335 --> 32:44.128
and it puts a smile on your face.

32:45.338 --> 32:46.172
‪Tada.

32:48.841 --> 32:49.968
Thank you for the food.

32:58.017 --> 33:00.061
The Park family's gimbap is so kkulmat.

33:03.773 --> 33:06.818
The takuan pickles
balance out the flavors perfectly.

33:06.901 --> 33:07.944
I wonder what it is…

33:08.695 --> 33:12.532
I feel like Korean takuan
has a more refreshing aftertaste.

33:15.368 --> 33:17.120
Maybe it has a stronger vinegar flavor.

33:17.996 --> 33:18.997
That's true.

33:20.164 --> 33:21.791
That's why it goes so well with rice.

33:23.251 --> 33:26.254
Sometimes we make them spicy
and eat it with rice too.

33:26.754 --> 33:28.214
It's called danmuji muchim.

33:28.798 --> 33:30.008
- I see.
- Yeah.

33:31.426 --> 33:34.053
That's danmu… danmu?

33:35.304 --> 33:37.515
Danmuji muchim.

33:37.598 --> 33:39.267
Da… danmujimuchim…

33:39.350 --> 33:42.103
- Danmuji muchim.
- Danmuji mu…?

33:42.186 --> 33:44.439
- Danmuji…
- Danmuji…?

33:44.522 --> 33:46.399
- muchim.
- muchim.

33:52.780 --> 33:54.407
That reminds me…

33:55.033 --> 33:56.492
How did it go with your brother?

33:58.953 --> 34:01.289
It didn't go well at all.

34:07.712 --> 34:11.299
But you kind of look
like a weight has been lifted.

34:12.675 --> 34:13.509
‪Yeah…

34:15.428 --> 34:17.847
In the end, I'm glad that I went.

34:18.598 --> 34:22.018
I was able to remember
things that I had forgotten too.

34:23.478 --> 34:24.771
Like what?

34:27.899 --> 34:29.400
Like how my mother made me

34:30.443 --> 34:33.613
onigiri every day
when I had club activities.

34:34.113 --> 34:35.531
- Every day?
- Yeah.

34:37.033 --> 34:40.244
I'm sure it was a lot of work for her too.

34:42.371 --> 34:44.624
Rather than thinking it's a lot of work,

34:44.707 --> 34:49.003
I think she just wanted to make sure
that you weren't hungry.

34:56.677 --> 34:59.347
When I was making gimbap earlier,

35:00.056 --> 35:01.933
that's what I was thinking.

35:03.017 --> 35:07.688
I wanted you to smile,
and say that it was delicious.

35:09.524 --> 35:12.193
I'm sure your mother was the same.

35:14.695 --> 35:16.030
Maybe…

35:17.240 --> 35:19.742
I understand that feeling too.

35:21.285 --> 35:22.161
I…

35:23.079 --> 35:25.414
wasn't able to live up to my
family's expectations.

35:26.249 --> 35:29.669
So I think I always had feelings of guilt.

35:31.754 --> 35:34.257
Family's expectations?

35:36.717 --> 35:38.261
I don't think that's right!

35:40.012 --> 35:41.597
What? What does that mean?

35:42.348 --> 35:44.225
I don't think it's right to push your

35:44.308 --> 35:46.727
expectations on people,
or choose their future for them.

35:52.441 --> 35:53.651
Sorry…

35:54.569 --> 35:57.280
Taiga, sorry for calling you
on your day off.

35:57.363 --> 35:58.865
The thing is, just now

35:58.948 --> 36:02.326
I got a call from the hospital
saying that my older sister collapsed.

36:03.077 --> 36:03.953
What?

36:04.537 --> 36:08.541
If possible, can you take care
of the restaurant for two or three days?

36:13.838 --> 36:16.090
Here's the flying squid sautéed
in butter and soy sauce.

36:16.924 --> 36:18.634
- Excuse me.
- Yes?

36:18.718 --> 36:21.012
- One oolong highball please.
- Okay.

36:27.059 --> 36:27.977
Welcome.

36:28.561 --> 36:30.146
Working hard?

36:31.981 --> 36:33.608
It looks like your own restaurant!

36:33.691 --> 36:35.776
Oh, he is someone who is
always helping me.

36:35.860 --> 36:37.278
Mr. Sakumoto.

36:37.361 --> 36:39.238
Hello, I'm Sakumoto.

36:41.699 --> 36:42.950
Have a seat over here.

36:53.252 --> 36:55.296
- Here's your stewed Koya-dofu.
- Here it is!

36:55.379 --> 36:56.547
- Enjoy.
- Thanks.

36:57.340 --> 36:59.800
The appetizer has a good kick to it
and is delicious.

37:01.177 --> 37:03.346
- Thank you.
- Wow, Taiga.

37:03.429 --> 37:06.432
Mr. Sakumoto is an expert
when it comes to food.

37:07.308 --> 37:10.436
- Is this Korean style?
- Yes.

37:11.187 --> 37:12.647
It's called danmuji muchim.

37:12.730 --> 37:16.400
I mixed Korean takuan
with garlic and chili powder.

37:16.984 --> 37:21.113
At the end, I added a bit of sesame oil
to bring the flavors together.

37:25.326 --> 37:29.789
I had heard from Mr. Ito
that you were a former athlete.

37:30.289 --> 37:32.291
I think that it's amazing how you have

37:32.375 --> 37:34.168
found another path for yourself

37:34.252 --> 37:37.088
even after ending
your career as an athlete.

37:37.838 --> 37:39.840
It's not something that everyone can do.

37:40.549 --> 37:42.301
Please continue to do your best.

37:44.679 --> 37:46.222
Thank you very much.

37:47.723 --> 37:49.100
Try the Koya-dofu.

37:51.060 --> 37:54.730
‪TANOMI

37:57.483 --> 37:59.193
Thank you for treating me.

38:00.820 --> 38:02.196
Thank you very much.

38:03.572 --> 38:05.157
I'm sorry I couldn't give this earlier…

38:09.412 --> 38:11.789
I work for a company called
Neo Meal Japan,

38:11.872 --> 38:15.293
and specialize in nutrition planning
and meal management for athletes.

38:15.793 --> 38:16.877
I see…

38:17.753 --> 38:19.672
- I hope to see you again.
- Bye.

38:20.840 --> 38:21.882
Thank you.

38:33.686 --> 38:35.396
- Taiga?
- Huh?

38:35.479 --> 38:36.522
PREVIEW

38:36.605 --> 38:38.649
Are you proposing
to Onigiri Man or something?

38:38.733 --> 38:40.693
You don't care if we're far apart, do you?

38:40.776 --> 38:43.029
‪THIS DRAMA IS FICTION AND ALL CHARACTERS
‪AND ORGANIZATIONS ARE FICTIONAL

38:43.112 --> 38:43.988
Subtitle translation by: Kiko Morita
